{"name":"Shortgrass Prairie","hex":"#9e957c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shortgrass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The set of short, tough grasses that thrive in arid plains; often specifically the native grasses of the North American Great Plains."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shortgrass"},{"term":"prairie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extensive area of relatively flat grassland with few, if any, trees, especially in North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prairie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shortgrass prairie","blocks":[{"text":"The shortgrass prairie is an ecosystem located in the Great Plains of North America. The two most dominant grasses in the shortgrass prairie are blue grama and buffalograss, the two less dominant grasses in the prairie are greasegrass and sideoats grama. The prairie was formerly maintained by grazing pressure of American bison, which is the keystone species. Due to its semiarid climate, the shortgrass prairie receives on average less precipitation than that of the tall and mixed grass prairies to the east."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Llano_Estacado_Caprock_Escarpment_south_of_Ralls_TX_2009.jpg/330px-Llano_Estacado_Caprock_Escarpment_south_of_Ralls_TX_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shortgrass_prairie","wikidata":"Q7502172"},{"title":"Prairie","blocks":[{"text":"Prairies are ecosystems considered part of the temperate grasslands, savannas, and shrublands biome by ecologists, based on similar temperate climates, moderate rainfall, and a composition of grasses, herbs, and shrubs, rather than trees, as the dominant vegetation type. Temperate grassland regions include the Pampas of Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay, and the steppe of Romania, Ukraine, Russia, and Kazakhstan. Lands typically referred to as \"prairie\" tend to be in North America. The term encompasses the lower and mid-latitude of the area referred to as the Interior Plains of Canada, the United States, and Mexico. It includes all of the Great Plains as well as the wetter, hillier land to the east. From west to east, generally the drier expanse of shortgrass prairie gives way to mixed grass prairie and ultimately the richer and wetter soils of the tallgrass prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg/330px-James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prairie","wikidata":"Q194281"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Shortgrass_pano_Petrified_Forest_NP.jpg/500px-Shortgrass_pano_Petrified_Forest_NP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Shortgrass_pano_Petrified_Forest_NP.jpg/1280px-Shortgrass_pano_Petrified_Forest_NP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Shortgrass_pano_Petrified_Forest_NP.jpg/500px-Shortgrass_pano_Petrified_Forest_NP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shortgrass prairie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShortgrass_pano_Petrified_Forest_NP.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Mom_and_Calf_%284819440992%29.jpg/500px-Mom_and_Calf_%284819440992%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Mom_and_Calf_%284819440992%29.jpg/500px-Mom_and_Calf_%284819440992%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bison mother and calf grazing on the prairie.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F